<h1>What's New With The ISFDB (1999)</h1>

<hr>

<dl><dt><b> 20 September 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> <i>Amazing Stories</i> is now complete.
   <li> <i>A. Merrit Fantasy Magazine</i> is now complete.
   <li> <i>Thrilling Wonder Stories</i> is now complete.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 7 September 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Exceeded 95,000 titles.
   <li> <i>Weird Tales</i> is now complete.
   <li> <i>Wonder Stories</i> is now complete.
   <li> <i>Thrilling Wonder Stories</i> is now complete through 1940.
   <li> <i>Amazing</i> is now complete from 1926 through 1949.
   </font>
 </ul>
<hr>
<p>
<dt><b> 16 August 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Added the ability to display cover art when displaying the contents
   of a book or magazine. The Engine is now Rev 1.12. All we need now is
   someplace to store cover art.
   <li> Added several hundred issues of various magazines. We now have
   complete runs of <i>The Magazine of Fantasy and Science Fiction</i>
   and <i>Analog/Astounding</i>.
   <li> Added 1876 titles, including 1329 short stories, 210 serials, 
   and 213 essays.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 9 August 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Exceeded 90,000 titles.
   <li> Added 5 issues of <i>Astounding</i>, completing the run from 1930
   through 1943.
   <li> Added all 11 issues of <i>Air Wonder Stories</i>, which ran from
   1929 through 1930.
   <li> Added 31 issues of <i>Amazing</i>, from 1930 thru 1934.
   <li> Added 633 titles, including 124 novels, 12 collections, 
   260 essays, 173 short stories, and 268 reviews.
   </font>
 </ul>

<hr>

<dt><b> 26 July 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Added 464 titles, including 229 novels, 10 collections, 
   59 essays, 179 short stories, and 36 reviews.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 19 July 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Got caught up on recent issues of <i>Amazing</i>.
   <li> Got caught up with reviews from <i>Science Fiction Weekly</i>.
   <li> Got caught up with reviews from <i>SF Site</i> through the
   end of 1998.
   <li> Added 571 titles, including 104 novels, 20 collections, 12 anthologies,
   78 essays, 324 short stories, and 191 reviews.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 12 July 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Got caught up on <i>Asimov's</i> and <i>NYRSF</i>.
   <li> Added 547 titles, including 102 novels, 18 collections,
   15 anthologies, 83 essays, 427 short stories, and 346 reviews.
   <li> Removed a lot of broken user-submitted data that cannot be
   verified anywhere.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 07 July 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Since John Boston knocked himself out over the 4th of July weekend, 
   I have made a special update with an all new Forthcoming Books section.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<dt><b> 06 July 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Added 2 issues of <i>A. Merritt's Fantasy Magazine</i>.
   <li> Added 2 issues of <i>Coven 13</i>.
   <li> Added 3 issues of <i>Fantastic Story Magazine</i>.
   <li> Added 29 issues of <i>Future Science Fiction</i>.
   <li> Added 34 issues of <i>Imagination</i>.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>

<hr>

<dt><b> 28 June 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <font size=-1>
   <li> Look's like I wasn't really back in January. Let's see what
   happens this time around.
   <li> I've sent around email, trying to round up the old crew. We should
   have a first update to forthcoming books this coming weekend.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
<hr>

<dt><b> 4 January 1999:</b>
 <ul>
   <li>
   <font size=-1>
 I'm back after a lengthy break. Expect an update to the awards, forthcoming
 books, as well as some catching up on recent magazine content over the next
 couple of weeks.
   <li>
 Apologies to those who've sent email over the last few months and received
 nothing in response. I've been pretty much unavailable, so I'll try to catch up
 now with those still interested.
   <li>
 I know that the author bio submissions have been broken for some time now.
 We'll try to fix things, but I'm not making any promises about when.
   </font>
 </ul>
<p>
</dl>

